{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266185,"nonce":"sBP+2oJolu9j5X8cO2xYFsE3viM=","message":"HANDOFF: room library, paused 2026-09-24 at the coordinator's request, to save tokens. It resumes later.\n\nWHERE IT STANDS\n- Branch: spec/bac4eba-room-library. Worktree: /home/dorian/projects/rimworld/autorimmer/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa901ce44e27479a1\n- No commits. The branch sits at 769fdd5 (main), and no file has been written. The research is done; this comment is its only copy.\n- Templates drafted on disk: none. Rotation checker written: no, but designed (below).\n\nSOURCE-VERIFIED FINDINGS (decompiled 1.6 and the bench Defs, by member name)\n1. A crashlanded start pre-completes ComplexFurniture, PassiveCooler, Stonecutting, ComplexClothing, Electricity, NutrientPaste and AirConditioning. Factions_Player.xml: PlayerColony startingResearchTags ClassicStart.\n   - Not pre-completed: Batteries, Firefoam, HospitalBed, VitalsMonitor, Smithing, Machining, TubeTelevision, MicroelectronicsBasics.\n   - Bed needs ComplexFurniture, through SansComfortBedBase. So INDEX's \"bedroom: research none\" is wrong as written, though true in effect at a crashlanded start.\n   - Shelf, EndTable, Dresser, DiningChair, ChessTable, Sarcophagus and Vent also need ComplexFurniture.\n   - No research: tables, Stool, TorchLamp, FueledStove, TableButcher, SimpleResearchBench, TableSculpting, HorseshoesPin, AnimalSleepingSpot, AnimalBed.\n2. DoubleBed is 2x2. bedroom.md's \"same footprint\" variant line is wrong.\n3. 16 benches carry workTableNotInRoomRoleFactor 0.8 (StatPart_WorkTableRoomRole). They include both stoves, both research benches, tailoring, stonecutter, sculptor and smithy. A bench outside a room of its own role works at 80%.\n   - Kitchen scores 28 per stove and Workshop 27 per bench, so one stove next to one bench makes a Kitchen.\n   - StatPart_WorkTableTemperature: benches work at 70% below 9 C or above 35 C.\n4. TableButcher has a null workTableRoomRole and Cleanliness -15. Butcher recipes have no products, so it does not score Kitchen.\n5. TorchWallLamp is Core and needs no research, but it has Placeworker_AttachedToWall. It would fail place-layout's preflight, which checks against a map that does not yet hold the layout's own walls. Use TorchLamp.\n6. Door and Cooler carry canPlaceOverWall, and Wall carries isPlaceOverableWall, so GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintOver lets a door or cooler go over a wall. This is the basis of the shared-wall rule below.\n7. PlaceWorker_Cooler.AllowsPlacing refuses if the cold cell (South.RotatedBy) or the hot cell (North.RotatedBy) is impassable. The hot side must vent outside the template, and ideally outdoors: Building_Cooler efficiency is 1 - dT/130.\n8. IncidentWorker_ShortCircuit.CanFireNowSub needs a ThingsOfDef(PowerConduit). So a base that uses only HiddenConduit, with generators and batteries as the other transmitters, has no Zzzt site at all.\n9. Rec room constraints:\n   - HorseshoesPin throws from exactly 5 cells away (watchBuildingStandDistanceRange 5~5), across a 3-wide rect, from inside the same room.\n   - HoopstoneRing and GameOfUrBoard are maxTechLevelToBuild Neolithic, so a crashlanded colony cannot build them.\n   - ChessTable needs a sittable cardinally adjacent (JoyGiver_InteractBuildingSitAdjacent).\n10. Dining: Toils_Ingest.TryFindChairOrSpot needs a sittable cardinally adjacent to a surfaceType Eat edifice. AteWithoutTable fires when the eater is not facing an eat surface. AteInImpressiveDiningRoom uses the impressiveness of whatever room the pawn eats in, regardless of that room's role.\n11. BedUtility.GetSlotPos puts a bed's head on the side opposite its Rot4: minZ at North, maxZ at South, minX at East, maxX at West.\n12. Building_Door.PawnCanOpen refuses FenceBlocked (pen) animals at a plain door unless they are roped. A barn with a plain door admits roaming animals only.\n13. RoomTempTracker equalizes temperature through walls into the rooms beyond. A generator or stove heats its neighbours, and a freezer chills its own.\n14. Room.ContainedAndAdjacentThings counts things set in the wall (coolers, doors) for both rooms, but not furniture in the neighbouring room.\n15. Rotation math:\n   - The game's rule is GenAdj.OccupiedRect with AdjustForRotation. North shifts nothing. East shifts z-1 when the rotated z is even. South shifts x-1 and z-1 on even axes. West shifts x-1 when the rotated x is even.\n   - This is rigid under quarter turns. I checked it by hand for Bed, SchoolDesk and FueledStove.\n   - A clockwise quarter turn maps (r,c) to (c, h-1-r) and adds 1 to the Rot4. A multi-cell token is re-anchored at its rotated footprint's north-west cell.\n   - The function needs each def's size and rotatable flag. The bench's catalog.json 'defs' already carries size, rotatable, interactionCells and passability.\n\nDRAFT DESIGN (nothing written yet)\nSize classes and contents:\n- Quarters:\n  - bedroom: Bed with its head at the back wall, torch by the door. The end table and dresser are a comfort pass, given as cells in the .md.\n  - kitchen: FueledStove_West along the side wall, torch.\n  - prison cell.\n  - tomb: 3 Sarcophagus.\n  - barn: 4 AnimalSleepingSpot and a torch.\n  - power room: WoodFiredGenerator against the front wall. The upgrades are batteries touching the generator and a popper, which comes within 3 of both.\n- Halves:\n  - barracks: 8 Beds.\n  - dining room: Table2x4c with 8 Stools. DiningChair is the upgrade.\n  - rec room: HorseshoesPin and a ChessTable with 2 Stools.\n  - hospital: 4 Beds to be flagged Medical. HospitalBed has the same 1x2 footprint, and VitalsMonitor cells sit between bed pairs.\n  - laboratory: 2 SimpleResearchBench. It is a half because the 5x2 HiTechResearchBench cannot fit a quarter.\n  - workshop: hand tailor, stonecutter and sculptor on one long wall, with smithy and machining cells on the other.\n  - prison barracks: 4 beds.\n  - storeroom: 8 Shelves.\n  - freezer: 2 Cooler_South in the long wall near its front, TableButcher at the far end, and no torch, because a torch heats below 23 C.\n  - classroom: the board and 4 desks in one row fit 9x4.\n  - hall: a new circulation module.\n\nCIRCULATION PROPOSAL (draft, for Dorian)\n- Rooms open onto hall halves, and every room has one door on its front side.\n- The door takes the cell immediately left of the side's centre, as seen from inside the room. On a 4-cell side that is the 2nd cell from the left, and on a 9-cell side the 4th.\n  - The rule is stated in the room's own frame, so rotation preserves it. The library never mirrors.\n  - A door never lands on a corner-adjacent cell or on a junction cell (the 5th of 9).\n- Shared walls: a wall-replacer (a Door or Cooler, flagged canPlaceOverWall) beats Wall, and a cell that already holds the same def counts as done.\n- There are no room-to-room doors. The freezer opens onto the hall, which retires \"the freezer's only door is into the kitchen\": that route sends every food haul across the kitchen floor.\n- Power rides the hall. It carries HiddenConduit under both long walls as layer 1, placed when the first powered room goes in.\n  - Rooms keep powered things within 6 cells of their front wall; this is BestTransmitterForConnector's ExpandedBy(6).\n  - A generator touches the trunk directly, so the library has no PowerConduit and no Zzzt site.\n- Halves front on a short end, so they attach along a spine. Quarters front on any side.\n- Worked 2x2 example:\n  - The spine is two hall halves in the east halves of the NW and SW squares. Their doors face north, and the north one is the exterior door.\n  - West quarters: bedrooms in NW-NW, NW-SW and SW-NW, and the kitchen in SW-SW, all fronting east.\n  - East halves: workshop in NE-N, dining in NE-S, storeroom or rec room in SE-N, and the freezer in SE-S, all fronting west.\n  - The freezer's coolers sit on the block's south perimeter. The kitchen and freezer doors face each other across the hall.\n- Why this layout: a single horizontal hall row in a 2x2 block leaves two halves unreachable, while a vertical spine leaves none.\n\nROTATION CHECKER PLAN\n- baseviz/rotate.py, under 200 lines, with rotate_ir(ir, k, defs), check_ir(ir, defs) and a command-line entry: python3 -m baseviz.rotate templates/*.ir.json. It reads templates/defs.json, a subset taken from the catalog, and --catalog cross-checks that subset.\n- Checks, in each of the 4 rotations:\n  - The size class is exactly 6x6, 11x6, 11x11 or 21x11, or one of those turned.\n  - Rotatable tokens carry a Rot4, and footprints neither overlap nor leave the grid.\n  - The outer ring is Wall, Door or Cooler, with Wall on the corners.\n  - Each door's inside cell is free. Each interaction cell is inside the room, on free floor, and shared with no other.\n  - A cooler's cold cell is inside the room and its hot cell outside the template.\n  - Every interaction cell is reachable from a door, and powered things are within 6 of the front wall.\n- Across rotations: rotating by k and back reproduces the original, and footprints and interaction cells map rigidly.\n- It also prints each template's Space, as 1.4 per standable cell plus 0.5 per walkable one.\n\nNEXT STEPS\n1. Work in the worktree on spec/bac4eba-room-library.\n2. Write rotate.py and defs.json, and commit them.\n3. Write the 17 template pairs. Re-cut the 5 existing ones, keeping or retiring each lesson with a stated reason: the old workshop's \"no benches\" and \"keep stoves out of the shell\" retire, and power-room's \"one deliberate PowerConduit\" gives way to the all-hidden trunk.\n4. Update INDEX: rows, the deferred DLC roles, the proposal and the worked example. Build the contact-sheet PNG with baseviz/png.py. Commit by function.\n\nOPEN QUESTIONS\n1. Should halves front on a short end (as chosen) or a long side?\n2. Is it right to retire the \"freezer only through the kitchen\" lesson?\n3. What should the hall trunk cost? Both long walls take 22 HiddenConduit per hall half (44 steel, about 6160 work); one wall halves that.\n4. Classroom is a Biotech role, but it is kept as a re-cut because the languages tests use it.\n5. Verb gap: no shipped verb flags a bed Medical or ForPrisoners; Source has no \".Medical =\" and no \"ForPrisoners =\". The hospital and prison templates need both. This is for the orchestrator to file; the prison side sits with e1c072e.","files":null}]}